  "subject": {
    "id": "domain-history-profile-runnable-examples",
    "type": "DOCUMENT"
  },
  "summary": "Bind byte-reproducible population examples to the full domain-history profiles.",
  "why": "The earlier handover examples still encoded the retired five-field profile and a source date as whole-batch valid time. The corrected archive uses the public compiler, exact shipped profile identities, ORDER_ONLY capture-import time, and committed raw reading and capture bytes. Tests compile, prepare, admit, reopen, replay, and trace those bytes without replacing profile identities or time values in memory."
